{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789319729,"nonce":"exAAZVuME4jER9deNHoaiFukqy0=","message":"Measured on the NUC (4 cores, aot_bench): the profile moves AOT method_call 120-122ms -\u003e 69.5-70.2 and nothing else in the corpus (it holds one entry for method_call, two for deltablue, none for closure_call). A profile-free guess of the STATIC receiver type's own implementation reproduces that number but the corpus survey says it is the wrong candidate at 62% of HOBJ/HSTRUCT dispatch sites (abstract-base pattern: the static type's implementation is a stub no allocated class reaches; deltablue 25 of 27 sites), i.e. a guard with no upside there. Landed instead: rapid type analysis (crates/ash/src/devirt.rs) -- the candidates are the distinct implementations the slot reaches through the classes the program allocates (any New) in the receiver's subtree, guarded when there are one or two. AOT method_call 70.8ms without a profile; deltablue unchanged (7.2 vs 7.3); guarded sites 28 (was 56 with the static guess) in method_call's program and 67 (was 83) in deltablue; AOT conformance 1069/1069. The CI lane stays profile-free. ASH_AOT_NO_STATIC_DEVIRT=1 turns the guess off.","files":null}]}